**[Suggestion]** Code duplication — extract a shared helper

This 25-line block is byte-identical to the one at ~line 2614–2638, differing only in one comment word ("heuristic loop detection" vs "loop detection"). If the dispatch mechanism or input payload needs updating (as it does — see the Critical finding above), both sites must be patched in lockstep.

**Concrete cost:** A fix to one block that misses the other causes the two loop-detection paths to send inconsistent payloads for the same `StopFailure` event.

**Suggested fix:** Extract a private method:
```typescript
private async fireLoopDetectionStopFailure(
  hooksEnabled: boolean,
  messageBus: MessageBus | undefined,
  loopType: string | null,
  signal: AbortSignal | undefined,
): Promise<void> {
  if (hooksEnabled && messageBus && this.config.hasHooksForEvent('StopFailure')) {
    await messageBus.request<HookExecutionRequest, HookExecutionResponse>(
      { type: MessageBusType.HOOK_EXECUTION_REQUEST, eventName: 'StopFailure',
        input: { error: 'loop_detected', error_details: loopType ?? undefined,
          last_assistant_message: this.getLastModelMessageText() || undefined },
        signal },
      MessageBusType.HOOK_EXECUTION_RESPONSE,
    );
  }
}
```

