**[Suggestion]** Duplicated backward scan for the last `recordId` — the same loop appears verbatim in `seed()` (here) and `seedReplayEvents()` (~line 321), differing only in the array variable name.

Failure scenario: if the scan logic needs to change (e.g. to skip certain event types or handle a new metadata path), it must be updated in two places — a one-site fix silently leaves the other path with old behavior, producing inconsistent anchors.

```suggestion
    this.activeRecordId = lastRecordIdIn(snapshot.compactedTurns);
```

Extract a shared helper:
```typescript
function lastRecordIdIn(events: BridgeEvent[]): string | undefined {
  for (let i = events.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    const id = replayRecordId(events[i]!);
    if (id !== undefined) return id;
  }
  return undefined;
}
```

